The clarification came from Christopher, because we asked in playtesting about Mass Levitation (because that would be amazing) and he clarified that anything that prevented environment cards from dealing damage would not stop this because it isn&#39;t dealt by a card.They could have used any wording but &quot;The Environment&quot; if they wanted a card to stop it, the whole idea is that it won&#39;t be affected by most easy methods.

[/quote]

Alright, official verdict it is.

&nbsp;

As for combos...

Did we ever fix the Friendly Fire + Jack Handle combo? &nbsp;Fixer deals damage to a target, Setback takes some damage, but Jack Handle turns the damage that would dealt to Setback into damage dealt to non-hero targets, which Setback can then use to take more damage... &nbsp;There was some discussion about fixing this because 2 card infinite combos make the game boring, but I can&#39;t remember if it actually happened.

Also, I don&#39;t think anyone&#39;s mentioned Bee Bot + End of Days yet. &nbsp;Use End of Days to destroy all unfriendly cards, then hit Bee Bot to kill End of Days before it destroys any hero cards.

&nbsp;

Dynamic Syphon + Cleansing Downpour: &nbsp;Whenever the Syphon takes damage, everybody heals 2 (including the Syphon). &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Hippocratic Oath + Proverbs and Axioms: &nbsp;3 Healing to two different hero targets? &nbsp;Why thank you! &nbsp;(Also, the Sentinels + Proverbs and Axioms is just kind of crazy in general, because you could potentially get 4 power uses out of it. &nbsp;And I don&#39;t think you need to use the power of the Sentinel who took damage)

